On Jul 10, 7:00 am, "Blog the Haggis" <NoS...@NoSpam.org> wrote:
> Hi All,
>
> I currently have a priest game where I have both a +7 Mjollnir and a +7
> Grayswandir and I was wondering which one I should use?
>
> From the spoilers it looks like Grayswandir does more damage at Expert level
> than Mjollnir but I'm restricted to Basic in saber. So the question is does
> Grayswandir at Basic do more damage than Mjollnir at Expert proficiency?
>
Grayswandir works against everything, Mjollnir doesn't.  Grayswandir
doesn't destroy monster inventory, Mjollnir does.  Mjollnir does bonus
damage regardless of its enchantment, so it's nice early on at +0--but
later on Mjollnir is a poor enough choice that I'll try to avoid
getting it if I'm a lawful Valk, since Excalibur is nice enough early
and very nice late.

Really the only artifact melee weapons I'd think about wielding over
Grayswandir are Magicbane (mostly for the curse resistance in the late
game and MR if I don't have a better source) and maybe occasionally
Sunsword/Excalibur/(Staff/Stormy/Vorpy/Tsurugi) in (very) special
cases--obviously missile weapons and some special-purpose non
artifacts (polearms, lance, bullwhip, etc) have their uses too.



